WEBVTT

00:00:53.003 --> 00:00:55.699
You and I will be reborn

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:57.740
In a future place and time

00:00:57.841 --> 00:01:03.211
If everything our
Hindu brethren say is true

00:01:04.114 --> 00:01:06.947
In an age of things that hover

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.917
You and I will still be lovers

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:11.776
And we'll say
to ourselves

00:01:11.922 --> 00:01:14.117
That was then and this is, too

00:01:14.224 --> 00:01:15.555
Doo-doo-be-doo, doo-doo

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.719
'Cause we'll still find
the happening hot spots

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:21.855
We'll still cruise the cool casinos

00:01:21.965 --> 00:01:24.433
You'll still fly me to the moon

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:26.661
Although the moon to which you fly me

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.567
Could be Phobos or Deimos

00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:31.140
The psychic worms from Rigel nine

00:01:31.241 --> 00:01:33.232
Who control everything we do

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.810
Will make us think that was then

00:01:34.911 --> 00:01:39.109
And 3010 is exactly the same as 1962

00:01:39.216 --> 00:01:41.650
Don't expect any changes, my friend

00:01:41.752 --> 00:01:46.086
That was then and this is, too

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:57.531
Wow, Mars Vegas.
Long live the eternal city.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:02:00.398
Two, one, zero!

00:02:03.473 --> 00:02:05.304
Rest in hell, Crapville!

00:02:12.182 --> 00:02:15.379
Out here in the desert,
we're gonna build bigger, better Vegas.

00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:18.943
Bathtubs size of oceans,
hookers size of bouncers.

00:02:19.056 --> 00:02:20.546
Hamburger!

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.694
Stand clear of the closing jaws.

00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:35.562
Yo, you need any
girders bent, I know a guy.

00:02:36.106 --> 00:02:37.767
So what's gonna
be over there, Dad?

00:02:37.874 --> 00:02:39.569
That? That the oasis.

00:02:40.977 --> 00:02:43.571
Future site of Oasis Hotel.

00:02:45.182 --> 00:02:48.242
Take that,
you stupid Mother Nature.

00:02:49.453 --> 00:02:51.853
Okay. Let's hit him hard.

00:02:52.055 --> 00:02:57.288
This land is your land
This land is my land

00:02:57.727 --> 00:02:59.388
Who are you noisy women?

00:02:59.696 --> 00:03:03.894
I'm Frida Waterfall, leader of the
Greenorita Eco-Feminist Collective,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.027
and we will not let you man-doze
this beautiful gyno-desert.

00:03:08.138 --> 00:03:10.800
Well, I'm Leo Wong, and I say, "Boom."

00:03:23.386 --> 00:03:27.618
Hey, what happened to my femi-necklace?
And where's my mega-fem?

00:03:30.861 --> 00:03:32.852
Is he badly hurt, Dr. Zoidberg?

00:03:33.029 --> 00:03:35.964
I don't quite know how to say this.

00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:38.964
Fry is dead!

00:03:43.673 --> 00:03:45.607
Wait, not dead.
The other thing.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:47.176
Damn eco-broads!

00:03:47.277 --> 00:03:50.872
You can't even spray for eagles
without upsetting these kooks.

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:56.911
Now, hang on.
Before you do construction,

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.989
don't you have to make sure
you're not harming any native species?

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.217
You mean, cursory
environmental survey?

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:04.350
Already done! By top scientist.

00:04:05.795 --> 00:04:09.162
Oh, my, yes.
You've got the go-ahead, Mr. Wong.

00:04:09.266 --> 00:04:11.530
This place is deader than last year's cat.

00:04:11.635 --> 00:04:12.932
No, it's not!

00:04:13.036 --> 00:04:16.403
There's precious life
right here in this scum puddle.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.129
Ah!

00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:21.540
Cyprinodon martius.
The desert muck leech.

00:04:21.645 --> 00:04:26.207
Amazingly, the entire species
lives in this one tiny stinkhole.

00:04:26.316 --> 00:04:30.116
Killing these will be so much easier
than exterminating those ponies.

00:04:34.858 --> 00:04:35.950
Wait a second.

00:04:36.059 --> 00:04:39.290
Leeches may not be
cuddly like pandas or tribbles,

00:04:39.396 --> 00:04:41.421
but these poor
endangered creatures deserve...

00:04:42.866 --> 00:04:44.333
Get off me!

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:48.564
I'll get it with my trusty foot cups:
Stompy and Smashy.

00:04:49.773 --> 00:04:52.367
No, don't kill it! We have to...

00:04:59.482 --> 00:05:02.417
There. They're not endangered anymore.
They're extinct.

00:05:03.653 --> 00:05:06.349
No, they're not. I saved this one.

00:05:06.456 --> 00:05:08.356
And I'm gonna raise it and care for it,

00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:10.449
so the world will
forever know what it's lost.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.222
You freaking slime wad!

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:20.692
No. I killed it.
It was the last of its kind.

00:05:22.038 --> 00:05:25.030
Mother.
Let go of me, you...

00:05:28.211 --> 00:05:29.542
Poor thing.

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:37.144
Tell you what, Fry.
You all promise not to sue me,

00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:40.951
I give you token for free
entry in poker tournament.

00:05:41.057 --> 00:05:42.490
He took it, you all saw it!

00:05:42.592 --> 00:05:46.460
Maybe we did, maybe we didn't.
What's in it for me, Bender?

00:05:46.796 --> 00:05:49.765
Okay, okay. Come back
when New Vegas opens,

00:05:49.866 --> 00:05:51.231
I give you all free rooms,

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:54.428
free dinner and
free tickets to Celine Dion.

00:05:54.537 --> 00:05:58.166
Lose the Celine Dion tickets
and you got yourself a deal.

00:05:59.509 --> 00:06:01.170
All right, damn it, done!

00:06:02.345 --> 00:06:03.403
All right, I scored.

00:06:12.789 --> 00:06:15.553
Look out, Vegas, I've got a system.

00:06:18.762 --> 00:06:19.751
Oh.

00:06:19.863 --> 00:06:21.057
I'm bankrupt.

00:06:21.164 --> 00:06:24.861
You said it, Hermes.
He is pathetic, but lovable.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:27.562
Yup. What? I said no such thing, man.

00:06:27.671 --> 00:06:32.040
I am not acting weird, Leela.
Why is everyone talking at once?

00:06:32.142 --> 00:06:34.133
Fry, calm down and stop braining.

00:06:34.244 --> 00:06:35.541
Yeah, Fry, maybe you need...

00:06:35.645 --> 00:06:38.409
You're right, Amy!
Maybe I do need some fresh air.

00:06:40.016 --> 00:06:41.950
Man, I'm worried about him.

00:06:42.052 --> 00:06:45.112
But not enough to stop
gambling for even a single second.

00:06:50.427 --> 00:06:51.655
You win, damn it!

00:06:54.064 --> 00:06:56.328
It's all in the wrist.

00:07:09.079 --> 00:07:10.478
Voices always yelling.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:14.914
Who said that? I'm not insane.
Stop it. Stop talking in me!

00:07:16.186 --> 00:07:19.053
Voices bothering you, man?
I've been there.

00:07:19.155 --> 00:07:21.350
You need one of these doodangs.

00:07:22.592 --> 00:07:23.889
A foil hat?
Of course, he likes pastrami.

00:07:23.993 --> 00:07:26.587
What about the dog's testicles?

00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:31.360
Hey, it worked.
The voices stopped.

00:07:31.468 --> 00:07:34.335
They've got a huge
selection of carburetors...

00:07:34.437 --> 00:07:35.631
Hang on. Hang on.

00:07:40.777 --> 00:07:42.711
That's better. My name's Hutch.

00:07:42.812 --> 00:07:46.213
Hi, Hutch. So what's with the
obnoxious, shrieking voices?

00:07:46.316 --> 00:07:48.147
Are my fillings picking up The View?

00:07:48.251 --> 00:07:53.120
No, man. Truth is,
it's other people's thoughts.

00:07:53.223 --> 00:07:54.417
You're a mind reader.

00:07:56.493 --> 00:08:00.520
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Although, actually, it was sort of obvious.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:02.827
You don't believe me?
Take off the helmet.

00:08:02.932 --> 00:08:05.264
- I believe you.
- Seriously, do it.

00:08:07.103 --> 00:08:10.095
Testing, testing.
Do you read me?

00:08:10.407 --> 00:08:12.602
Loud and clear.
- What?

00:08:12.709 --> 00:08:14.768
I said, "Loud and clear."

00:08:14.878 --> 00:08:16.812
Only I said it with my
thinker, not my talker.

00:08:16.913 --> 00:08:20.747
Whoa! Freaky.
Why can't I read your thoughts?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.876
I don't know. Wait.
What's that about a secret society?

00:08:23.987 --> 00:08:28.424
Never mind that. Just keep
the foil on and you'll be okay.

00:08:28.525 --> 00:08:33.087
Also, it'll keep the Dark Ones
from incinerating your brain.

00:08:33.196 --> 00:08:34.163
That's a plus.

00:08:34.264 --> 00:08:37.859
And don't ever, ever, ever
tell anyone you can read minds,

00:08:37.967 --> 00:08:41.130
or the Dark Ones
will get you like that.

00:08:42.772 --> 00:08:44.740
Hang on, pizza grease.

00:08:45.141 --> 00:08:46.438
Like that.

00:09:04.727 --> 00:09:07.025
Jeez, get a load of
the batteries on her.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.064
I'd like to get my clamps on those.

00:09:09.165 --> 00:09:10.792
Give her a jump,
you know what I mean?

00:09:12.001 --> 00:09:12.990
Whoa, whoa.

00:09:13.102 --> 00:09:16.094
Show some decorum there,
Clamps. This ain't no strip show.

00:09:16.206 --> 00:09:19.642
This is a beguiling display
of the pornographic arts.

00:09:19.742 --> 00:09:22.210
Yo, Skip, I can see a guy's butt.

00:09:22.779 --> 00:09:26.943
Oh, Michael, this is the perfect
end to a perfect honeymoon.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:28.108
I love you so much.

00:09:29.285 --> 00:09:31.185
- Is this seat taken?
- Actually, we...

00:09:31.287 --> 00:09:33.152
Slide me those chicken wings.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.388
So what part of
Podunk you rubes from?

00:09:36.493 --> 00:09:37.517
The north-eastern.

00:09:55.245 --> 00:09:57.110
Monsieurs et mademoiselles,

00:09:57.213 --> 00:10:03.948
our circus of the senses now arrives
by steamboat in New Orleans, circa 2873.

00:10:04.053 --> 00:10:07.648
The muted lament of a trombone
resonates through the fog,

00:10:07.757 --> 00:10:12.694
which lingers even now, months
after the attack of the fog monster.

00:10:12.795 --> 00:10:16.458
With but one hope of restoring
Gearoticus to his throne,

00:10:16.566 --> 00:10:20.366
our sensual fate
rests in the gyrations of

00:10:21.137 --> 00:10:22.968
Fanny.

00:10:25.275 --> 00:10:26.299
Oh.

00:10:48.998 --> 00:10:49.987
Yes?

00:10:50.099 --> 00:10:51.760
I'm Bender. Let's do it.

00:10:59.509 --> 00:11:00.533
Who is it, the Feds?

00:11:00.643 --> 00:11:04.477
Aren't you the Donbot,
head of the Robot Mafia?

00:11:04.581 --> 00:11:07.516
Allegedly.
And this is my beloved wife, Fanny,

00:11:07.617 --> 00:11:10.347
whose honor I would
proudly defend with a power drill.

00:11:10.453 --> 00:11:12.614
Well, I gotta go drown a stoolie.

00:11:17.994 --> 00:11:21.828
I'm gonna be in here a while, so do
me a favor and drive my wife home.

00:11:22.765 --> 00:11:26.792
It's one of them self-driving cars, so
just sit in the back and do whatever.

00:11:30.073 --> 00:11:32.871
Oh, Bender,
your lips are intoxicating.

00:11:32.976 --> 00:11:36.207
It's like kissing
an ashtray full of hot wings.

00:11:48.858 --> 00:11:52.487
My God, I really can read minds.
I have a superpower!

00:11:52.862 --> 00:11:55.626
There must be something
great I can do with this.

00:12:00.269 --> 00:12:02.863
Hello, ladies,
I can read your thoughts.

00:12:06.342 --> 00:12:08.242
Oh, wait, that's invisibility.

00:12:12.782 --> 00:12:16.479
Poker. With my mind-reading
abilities and my invisibility...

00:12:16.586 --> 00:12:19.077
Wait, no, just the mind reading.
I can't lose!

00:12:19.956 --> 00:12:21.685
Sign me up for the tournament, please.

00:12:21.791 --> 00:12:26.023
Okey-doke, Jiffy Pop.
Entry fee's 50,000 smackers.

00:12:26.129 --> 00:12:27.357
50,000?

00:12:28.531 --> 00:12:30.522
Drat, all I have is my life savings

00:12:30.633 --> 00:12:34.194
and a token for free admission
to this poker tournament.

00:12:34.303 --> 00:12:35.531
Close enough.

00:12:42.045 --> 00:12:45.879
You're having an affair with
the head of the robot mafia's wife?

00:12:45.982 --> 00:12:48.246
Yup, this is
her I'm making out with.

00:12:50.453 --> 00:12:51.886
Bender, are you crazy?

00:12:51.988 --> 00:12:54.684
No, it's Fry who's crazy in this one.

00:12:54.791 --> 00:12:56.486
I'm not crazy.

00:12:56.592 --> 00:12:58.082
You sure you're okay, Fry?

00:12:58.194 --> 00:13:00.628
I mean, you do have
tin foil on your head.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.891
So? You got a leech on your neck.

00:13:02.999 --> 00:13:06.491
And speaking of sucking on your
neck, want to go to a movie later?

00:13:06.602 --> 00:13:09.070
Hey, there!
How are you folks doing tonight?

00:13:09.172 --> 00:13:10.867
Great. What are the specials?

00:13:10.973 --> 00:13:14.773
Well, let's see now.
We've got a wonderful grizzly bear

00:13:14.877 --> 00:13:17.311
that's been dipped in cornmeal
and lightly tormented.

00:13:17.413 --> 00:13:19.745
- Questions?
- What was the bear's name?

00:13:19.849 --> 00:13:22.579
- Jojo.
- Ooh, I'll have him.

00:13:25.688 --> 00:13:27.383
- Hide me!
- Hey, Donbot,

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.584
ain't that your wife what
with you had that wedding with?

00:13:30.893 --> 00:13:34.852
Donbot, honey!
What a pleasant shock!

00:13:34.964 --> 00:13:39.424
I was just having dinner alone,
when suddenly you walk in on us.

00:13:39.535 --> 00:13:40.593
Alone, huh?

00:13:44.207 --> 00:13:45.231
Where am I?

00:13:45.341 --> 00:13:50.278
I was exploring a wormhole through space
many light years from this restaurant,

00:13:50.379 --> 00:13:53.177
when suddenly I was
surrounded by darkness.

00:13:53.282 --> 00:13:54.977
Hot, sexy darkness.

00:13:56.319 --> 00:14:01.279
Why, hello, Donbot! Hello, miss,
have we met? I'm Bender.

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:03.858
The world's most sexual robot.

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:07.191
I mean, the world's most
boundary-respecting robot.

00:14:07.563 --> 00:14:10.930
Nice to see you, Bender.
Welcome back to our universe.

00:14:11.033 --> 00:14:13.831
Listen, sugar, I stuck up
the Burlington Coat Factory

00:14:13.936 --> 00:14:16.996
and got you a little something.
It's a $49 value.

00:14:18.641 --> 00:14:21.701
Donbot, I love you!

00:14:21.811 --> 00:14:24.541
- Not really.
- Man, this is great!

00:14:24.647 --> 00:14:28.174
I always wanted to nail a dame
in a fur coat, and now's my chance.

00:14:29.352 --> 00:14:34.153
I mean, if you'll introduce me to
one, sir. One as sexy as you, baby!

00:14:34.657 --> 00:14:35.851
Bender out.

00:14:43.733 --> 00:14:45.997
I never felt so alive, Bender.

00:14:46.102 --> 00:14:49.503
Listen, this turquoise-encrusted
bra is worth 50 grand.

00:14:49.605 --> 00:14:52.802
Let's sell it and run off
before the Donbot gets wise.

00:14:52.909 --> 00:14:57.937
No. It will take a lot more money
than that to make a girl like you happy.

00:14:58.047 --> 00:15:00.311
- No, it won't.
- Yeah, it will. Shut up!

00:15:00.416 --> 00:15:06.286
We'll run off, but not till after I win
the Universal Poker Championship!

00:15:08.024 --> 00:15:09.958
One entry, please.

00:15:10.059 --> 00:15:13.460
Bender, no! You can't beat
the best players in the universe.

00:15:13.563 --> 00:15:18.330
- You're not lucky enough.
- Oh, no? I'm 40% lucky.

00:15:18.434 --> 00:15:21.870
The scrap metal I'm made from
included a truckload of horseshoes

00:15:21.971 --> 00:15:26.237
from the luckiest racehorses in Mexico,
who had just been sent to a glue factory.

00:15:26.809 --> 00:15:30.768
- They don't sound so lucky to me.
- Not without their shoes.

00:15:40.623 --> 00:15:42.215
That's great!

00:15:47.363 --> 00:15:50.730
Here, Bendy, take this.
It will give you 70% more luck.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.600
It's the Donbot's lucky robot's foot.

00:15:53.703 --> 00:15:57.070
All right!
With two kinds of luck, I can't lose.

00:15:57.173 --> 00:15:59.573
No, wait, three.
I stepped on a leprechaun.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.640
Yo, you see this over here over there?

00:16:03.746 --> 00:16:05.646
I'm powering up the clamps.

00:16:08.818 --> 00:16:11.685
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Let us not rush to judgment.

00:16:11.787 --> 00:16:15.985
But, Skip, that was your lucky robot's
foot what came off of your lucky leg.

00:16:16.092 --> 00:16:19.619
While it is true that I did wake up
with only one foot this morning,

00:16:19.729 --> 00:16:22.721
there is no proof that my
beloved Fanny was involved.

00:16:22.832 --> 00:16:25.096
Aside from the hacksaw
I found under her pillow.

00:16:25.201 --> 00:16:28.500
Well, what about that Bender guy?
You want I should give him the clamps?

00:16:28.604 --> 00:16:32.597
Not yet, Clamps. Only one thing
can prove that he has my lucky foot.

00:16:32.708 --> 00:16:35.233
Torture with the clamps
or a clamp-like device?

00:16:35.611 --> 00:16:39.570
No. We are gonna sit tight and see
if he wins the poker tournament.

00:16:39.682 --> 00:16:42.378
He does, that proves
he's packing my lucky foot,

00:16:43.286 --> 00:16:44.548
in which event...

00:16:44.654 --> 00:16:46.053
The clamps!

00:16:47.857 --> 00:16:49.324
Or a clamp-like device.

00:16:53.195 --> 00:16:56.164
Welcome viewers
who fell asleep with the TV on!

00:16:56.265 --> 00:17:00.429
It's the 3009 no-limit
hold 'em championship.

00:17:03.039 --> 00:17:04.870
I'm the massive head
of Penn Jillette,

00:17:04.974 --> 00:17:08.000
and here with a color
commentary, my partner Teller.

00:17:09.145 --> 00:17:11.705
Our act really didn't
change much when he died.

00:17:11.814 --> 00:17:13.805
Pardon me,
I'm new to this game.

00:17:13.916 --> 00:17:16.316
Is this duffle bag big
enough for all your money?

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:20.618
Bender? Oh, boogers.
We're in the same tournament.

00:17:20.723 --> 00:17:22.953
Quick, get your entry fee
back before I bankrupt you.

00:17:23.059 --> 00:17:25.527
In your dreams, nutloaf.

00:17:26.729 --> 00:17:28.993
Bite my shiny metal hat.

00:17:34.437 --> 00:17:37.895
Tex Connecticut,
the pride of Kansas City, first to act.

00:17:39.608 --> 00:17:41.473
Smiley Spiff, up next.

00:17:45.181 --> 00:17:47.877
Looks like Boobs Vanderbilt
has a decent pair.

00:17:47.984 --> 00:17:49.747
Also, she's got two eights.

00:17:52.388 --> 00:17:56.119
And Bender Rodriguez picks
up a lucky deal right off the bat.

00:18:00.696 --> 00:18:04.325
Two aces.
I'm thinking guitar solo.

00:18:08.471 --> 00:18:09.438
I fold.

00:18:09.538 --> 00:18:14.168
Holy crap! A stunning play by
mentally ill newcomer Philip Fry.

00:18:14.276 --> 00:18:17.677
It's almost as if
he knew Bender had two aces.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:19.941
Bender has two aces? I'm out.

00:18:20.049 --> 00:18:21.516
- I'm out.
- I'm out.

00:18:23.052 --> 00:18:24.246
Suck my luck!

00:18:26.989 --> 00:18:28.513
See this gun?

00:18:29.558 --> 00:18:32.152
That's what I'm gonna
do to Bender if he wins.

00:18:41.404 --> 00:18:45.431
All in. Call my mighty bid at your peril.

00:18:48.778 --> 00:18:51.474
My cards are awful, and I need a hug.

00:18:52.348 --> 00:18:54.282
I call your bluff.

00:18:58.687 --> 00:19:00.450
I shall annihilate...

00:19:01.657 --> 00:19:05.491
I just wanted to
make my daddy proud.

00:19:06.062 --> 00:19:09.429
Well, you didn't. I want you and
your junk moved out by Monday.

00:19:09.665 --> 00:19:11.326
It's getting
pretty intense, folks.

00:19:11.434 --> 00:19:13.959
Based on the state of
decomposition of Teller's head,

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:16.766
we're now in hour
19 of the tournament.

00:19:16.872 --> 00:19:20.273
And the first bad deal
of the night for Bender.

00:19:20.376 --> 00:19:24.176
Hey, pal, help me out here.
This is the worst possible hand, right?

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:25.269
I'm all in.

00:19:25.381 --> 00:19:27.281
All in! I mean, fold. Whatever.

00:19:29.151 --> 00:19:33.781
Well, Bender's luck just ran out.
No card can save him from elimination.

00:19:35.858 --> 00:19:38.088
Oh, my gourds! He's dead.

00:19:39.762 --> 00:19:41.753
21, winner!

00:19:43.099 --> 00:19:46.899
I'm so full of luck,
it's shooting out like luck diarrhea.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:50.101
Wake up, poker fans!

00:19:50.206 --> 00:19:54.734
We're down to our final two players in
heads-up action for the Championship.

00:19:54.844 --> 00:19:56.869
Your perspective, Teller?

00:20:21.437 --> 00:20:23.029
All in.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.765
But you didn't even
look at your cards!

00:20:26.876 --> 00:20:31.370
Looking at one's cards is
a crutch for players who rely on skill.

00:20:37.686 --> 00:20:39.654
Any day now, Fry. You in or out?

00:20:42.958 --> 00:20:46.519
What's the matter, Fry,
you scared? Or just crazy?

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:50.189
All right, all in.

00:20:55.538 --> 00:20:58.200
Yes! Four aces!

00:20:58.307 --> 00:20:59.706
Ah-ah-ah.

00:20:59.808 --> 00:21:03.335
Read 'em and weep,
and then tell me what they are.

00:21:03.445 --> 00:21:08.144
Two kings. And with three on the board,
that gives Bender five kings.

00:21:09.885 --> 00:21:12.718
- But how is that...
- I don't believe it.

00:21:12.821 --> 00:21:15.722
Bender has just been
dealt the King of Beers,

00:21:15.824 --> 00:21:19.282
a coaster from the bar that
somehow got mixed into the deck.

00:21:19.495 --> 00:21:20.826
But it still counts!

00:21:22.865 --> 00:21:25.425
Bender win the Championship!

00:21:27.536 --> 00:21:29.003
That's some good money.

00:21:30.839 --> 00:21:34.935
You did it, Bender.
You're the greatest.

00:21:35.044 --> 00:21:36.875
Tell me something
I don't know, sweetass.

00:21:36.979 --> 00:21:37.968
Now, let's boogie.

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:41.914
We'll be in Space Tahiti before
the Donbot knows what hit him.

00:21:44.486 --> 00:21:46.511
Now I am suspicious.

00:21:55.464 --> 00:21:58.922
Okay, we finished digging this
shallow grave. Can we go now?

00:22:37.506 --> 00:22:40.066
Poor Bender left me one last voicemail

00:22:40.175 --> 00:22:43.906
before the Robot Mafia
buried him in the desert.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:48.208
Fry, old friend,
before I die, I just wanted to say...

00:22:49.451 --> 00:22:51.544
Hang on, I'm getting another call. Hello?

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:58.617
Line up, people! Everyone take
a shovel and one sixth of the planet.

00:22:58.727 --> 00:23:03.289
We'll meet back here in 50 years,
our bodies broken and our lives wasted.

00:23:03.399 --> 00:23:05.424
And you say these are free shovels?

00:23:12.408 --> 00:23:13.500
I'm back, baby.

00:23:13.609 --> 00:23:16.305
Bender! I thought the
Robot Mafia killed you.

00:23:16.412 --> 00:23:20.314
Nah, they just shot us and buried us
a few times as a warning.

00:23:20.416 --> 00:23:22.316
Bender was so brave.

00:23:22.418 --> 00:23:25.683
He never stopped making out with me
the whole time they were shooting us.

00:23:25.788 --> 00:23:27.016
I sure didn't.

00:23:27.589 --> 00:23:30.183
I gotta get back to my husband, baby.
Will I see you tonight?

00:23:30.292 --> 00:23:31.486
Probably not.

00:23:37.633 --> 00:23:42.332
It's a 14-footer with a clown hazard.
What club you recommend, Baggy?

00:23:42.438 --> 00:23:44.998
As on every hole,
I suggest the putter.

00:23:47.376 --> 00:23:50.971
Your golf club sure is classy,
Mr. Wong. Naked statue classy.

00:23:54.817 --> 00:23:56.307
It is very nice.

00:23:56.418 --> 00:24:00.445
I just wish Amy and I didn't have to
wear these sexist badges on our melons.

00:24:01.223 --> 00:24:03.657
We're lucky even to play as guests, Leela.

00:24:03.759 --> 00:24:06.956
Dad's club has a very
strict "No girls allowed" policy.

00:24:09.131 --> 00:24:11.599
- That doesn't seem fair.
- It really is.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:13.725
Everybody knows women
don't have the focus

00:24:13.836 --> 00:24:16.896
to play miniature golf
at a professional level.

00:24:18.140 --> 00:24:20.404
But that's the
best shot of the day!

00:24:20.509 --> 00:24:22.739
Is that my ball?
I think that my ball.

00:24:27.015 --> 00:24:29.813
- Great putt, Dad.
- Okay, we're done.

00:24:31.186 --> 00:24:34.644
Mr. Wong, how do you keep this place
so green in the middle of the desert?

00:24:34.757 --> 00:24:36.247
Doesn't that waste a lot of water?

00:24:36.358 --> 00:24:40.089
Nah, we got plenty water,
pumped directly from flamingo lake.

00:24:46.402 --> 00:24:47.994
They'll be fine.

00:24:50.806 --> 00:24:54.139
Oh, yeah, I love miniature golf.
Love everything about it,

00:24:54.243 --> 00:24:56.177
except how damn miniature it is.

00:24:56.278 --> 00:24:59.907
That's why I'm building the universe's
biggest miniature golf course.

00:25:04.186 --> 00:25:06.984
- This the first tee.
- Where's the hole?

00:25:07.089 --> 00:25:08.784
On Pluto's moon, Hydra.

00:25:08.891 --> 00:25:13.089
It's a six-billion-mile par-two.
Tough shot, even for a man.

00:25:28.944 --> 00:25:32.471
Around the sun.
Bank off Jupiter.

00:25:32.848 --> 00:25:35.009
And right into the...

00:25:37.686 --> 00:25:38.710
I'll be right back.

00:25:58.540 --> 00:26:00.667
It dropped in!
Put me down for a two.

00:26:02.077 --> 00:26:03.237
Two.

00:26:06.915 --> 00:26:09.543
Keep in mind,
that just the first hole.

00:26:09.651 --> 00:26:13.485
For full course, we gonna bulldoze
this entire arm of the Milky Way.

00:26:13.589 --> 00:26:18.288
What? You're gonna wipe out 10%
of the galaxy for a stupid golf course?

00:26:18.393 --> 00:26:21.829
First of all, it 12%.
Second, yes, you betcha.

00:26:21.930 --> 00:26:25.559
But you have no idea what life
forms might be evolving out there.

00:26:25.667 --> 00:26:28.363
That's exactly why
I'm hiring an impartial scientist

00:26:28.470 --> 00:26:32.031
to perform an environmental survey.
That's him in the money shower.

00:26:35.444 --> 00:26:39.608
Delivery boy's log. Having fallen
asleep on what I thought was the toilet,

00:26:39.715 --> 00:26:42.980
I awoke to find
the environmental survey in progress.

00:26:43.252 --> 00:26:48.349
- Status reports, Science Officer.
- Zilcho. No sign of life or intelligence.

00:26:52.661 --> 00:26:54.151
Just like Fry on a date.

00:26:54.263 --> 00:26:55.560
Hey!

00:26:55.664 --> 00:26:58.531
Okay, so we haven't
found any life yet.

00:26:58.634 --> 00:27:03.196
I still don't see why you men can't be
happy with regular-sized miniature golf.

00:27:03.572 --> 00:27:07.201
Leela, evolution has
programmed our fabulous male brains

00:27:07.309 --> 00:27:11.678
to take anything anybody else thinks
is important and make it bigger.

00:27:13.248 --> 00:27:16.775
Have you seen my new 301-inch TV?

00:27:16.885 --> 00:27:21.345
Hypnotoad is brought to
you by the MagnaPhallix 302-inch TV.

00:27:21.690 --> 00:27:23.157
It's bigger!

00:27:23.592 --> 00:27:24.559
Oh, hell!

00:27:28.497 --> 00:27:31.227
Captain, I'm detecting
life on the spock-o-scope!

00:27:47.716 --> 00:27:51.083
It's amazing. It's like
a textbook on evolution.

00:27:51.186 --> 00:27:52.210
Except in Kansas.

00:27:52.321 --> 00:27:54.949
But isn't Mr. Wong
building the 18th hole here?

00:27:55.057 --> 00:27:56.649
And the golf pants museum?

00:27:56.758 --> 00:28:00.159
Indeed so. This whole
area will be incinerated

00:28:00.262 --> 00:28:03.231
when he implodes that
sun there into a black hole.

00:28:03.365 --> 00:28:05.060
That beautiful violet star?

00:28:05.167 --> 00:28:08.500
It's so you can't keep
your ball at the end of the game.

00:28:08.604 --> 00:28:10.162
Yo, that's messed up.

00:28:10.272 --> 00:28:14.265
Well, there won't be any imploding once
they read our environmental review.

00:28:14.376 --> 00:28:17.072
- Right, Professor?
- Twaddle-squat.

00:28:17.179 --> 00:28:20.706
There's no scientific
consensus that life is important.

00:28:20.816 --> 00:28:22.613
Yeah. Life, schmife.

00:28:24.119 --> 00:28:26.610
Approved for demolition.

00:28:26.722 --> 00:28:28.485
It's you and me, ponytail.

00:28:36.632 --> 00:28:37.724
We're here, Mr. President.

00:28:39.434 --> 00:28:41.459
Let's play some mini-golf.

00:28:42.037 --> 00:28:46.098
Now, just give it a light tap, Agnew.
No, no, no, just a light...

00:28:49.578 --> 00:28:51.876
Now for a triple clam dip, with a double...

00:28:51.980 --> 00:28:53.004
Ow!

00:28:56.852 --> 00:29:01.482
Tough luck, Agnew. Looks like you
and Wong owe me a Charleston Chew.

00:29:06.094 --> 00:29:08.085
- Shut up and hear our wisdom.
- Shut up and hear our wisdom.

00:29:08.196 --> 00:29:10.096
- Save the ecosystem.
- Save the ecosystem.

00:29:10.198 --> 00:29:13.827
Shut up and hear
our wisdom! Save the ecosystem!

00:29:14.202 --> 00:29:17.137
What gives, Wong?
You said no chicks allowed.

00:29:18.774 --> 00:29:21.834
We are the Greenorita
Eco-Feminist Collective,

00:29:21.943 --> 00:29:25.379
and we will not let you...
What was it again?

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:28.608
We will not let you implode
the violet dwarf star

00:29:28.717 --> 00:29:35.054
at galactic coordinates
167.84, -58.03, mark 948.

00:29:35.357 --> 00:29:37.621
Already approved, you cackling hens.

00:29:37.726 --> 00:29:41.229
So get out, or I'll have vice-president
Agnew's headless body throw you out.

00:29:41.496 --> 00:29:43.430
I'd like to see him try.

00:29:43.532 --> 00:29:46.558
Me, too. Should look funny.
Sic 'em, Agnew.

00:29:51.506 --> 00:29:53.633
Runaway golf cart!

00:29:53.742 --> 00:29:55.437
Look out, Agnew!

00:29:57.779 --> 00:29:58.871
- Whoa!
- Aah!

00:30:02.617 --> 00:30:04.608
Is he okay?

00:30:05.754 --> 00:30:07.119
No pulse.

00:30:07.723 --> 00:30:12.422
They killed the headless
remains of Agnew. Arrest them!

00:30:14.596 --> 00:30:17.861
All feministas
she-vacuate the premises.

00:30:17.966 --> 00:30:19.593
I mean "femises."

00:30:29.478 --> 00:30:31.378
My fellow Earthicans,

00:30:31.480 --> 00:30:35.007
these eco-crooks will
face the maximum sentence.

00:30:35.117 --> 00:30:37.779
For killing a headless
torso, that's six weeks.

00:30:38.019 --> 00:30:39.543
Well, this is embarrassing.

00:30:39.654 --> 00:30:43.317
Here I've been blabbing on
for years about killing all humans,

00:30:43.425 --> 00:30:46.189
and who actually does
something about it? Some chick.

00:30:46.294 --> 00:30:49.195
Leela's not a killer,
and she's not some chick.

00:30:49.297 --> 00:30:51.026
She's the chick I love.

00:30:51.133 --> 00:30:53.567
And don't tell her
I called her a chick, or she'll kill me.

00:31:08.650 --> 00:31:11.050
Everyone stay absolutely quiet!

00:31:11.153 --> 00:31:12.313
- That thing's on.
- Turn it off!

00:31:12.420 --> 00:31:13.444
Oh, sorry.

00:31:13.555 --> 00:31:15.420
How do you turn it off?

00:31:15.524 --> 00:31:17.151
There. Did that do it?

00:31:17.259 --> 00:31:18.453
No. Stop it. Shut up.

00:31:18.560 --> 00:31:20.528
Here's the button here.

00:31:22.264 --> 00:31:23.891
And I think I... Now I got it.

00:31:25.367 --> 00:31:26.994
Let me give you a hand.

00:31:28.837 --> 00:31:30.031
This is awful.

00:31:30.138 --> 00:31:33.767
I never meant for our protest to
have any effect. Now what do we do?

00:31:33.875 --> 00:31:36.935
Maybe we should just surrender
and serve our six weeks in jail.

00:31:37.045 --> 00:31:40.606
Hey, yeah! We could do each
other's toenails and make shivs.

00:31:42.717 --> 00:31:45.185
That's crazy.
We've done nothing wrong,

00:31:45.287 --> 00:31:48.313
other than killing and
dismembering the vice-president.

00:31:48.423 --> 00:31:50.516
We need to make a choice, sisters.

00:31:50.625 --> 00:31:54.789
We can either keep pestering criminals
like Leo Wong with silly slogans...

00:31:54.896 --> 00:31:56.488
- Yeah.
- Let's do that.

00:31:57.065 --> 00:32:00.523
Actually, I meant that to be
the less preferable alternative.

00:32:00.635 --> 00:32:05.732
We can either chant slogans
or we can take action.

00:32:05.841 --> 00:32:07.433
What was the first choice again?

00:32:07.542 --> 00:32:12.479
I choose to save the environment by
sabotaging Leo Wong's golf course.

00:32:12.581 --> 00:32:14.208
Who's with me?

00:32:15.650 --> 00:32:17.083
Could we still use our bullhorns?

00:32:17.185 --> 00:32:18.311
Absolutely.

00:32:18.420 --> 00:32:21.048
Bullhorns are a core
principle of eco-feminism.

00:32:21.156 --> 00:32:22.214
Then I'm in.

00:32:25.627 --> 00:32:27.857
Uh, take that

00:32:27.963 --> 00:32:29.362
Yeah, yeah

00:32:29.464 --> 00:32:31.091
Uh-huh, uh-huh, yeah

00:32:31.199 --> 00:32:33.793
Izzy, Izzy, ah
Zizah, zizah, zizah

00:32:33.902 --> 00:32:36.268
Girls be talkin'
Like they all rah, rah

00:32:36.738 --> 00:32:39.138
Who's ready to kick
some sweaty man-butt?

00:32:41.109 --> 00:32:44.169
I've got my pointy
man-kicking shoes on.

00:32:44.279 --> 00:32:45.405
Those are cute.

00:32:45.513 --> 00:32:47.674
Aren't they?
I got them at Nine West.

00:32:47.782 --> 00:32:50.808
Simmer down, warriors.
Full power to the vagyroscope!

00:33:00.562 --> 00:33:01.961
Those dirty rings.

00:33:02.063 --> 00:33:04.827
I tried soaking them out,
even blasting them out.

00:33:13.375 --> 00:33:14.569
Are you sure about this?

00:33:14.676 --> 00:33:18.305
It would be better for propaganda
if we weren't using refined sugar.

00:33:18.413 --> 00:33:22.315
It's okay. The potato we're
shoving in the tailpipe is organic.

00:33:28.723 --> 00:33:30.520
I smell sabotage.

00:33:31.860 --> 00:33:33.054
And potatoes.

00:33:36.865 --> 00:33:40.323
Now, unfortunately, the media is
going to put a negative spin on this,

00:33:40.435 --> 00:33:41.800
like when we killed that guy,

00:33:41.903 --> 00:33:45.168
so to win public support,
we'll need a lovable mascot.

00:33:51.212 --> 00:33:54.010
Squirm all you want,
you nasty dumpling.

00:33:54.149 --> 00:33:57.414
One less species for the universe,
one more breakfast for...

00:33:57.519 --> 00:34:00.010
- Zoidberg?
- Leela.

00:34:00.121 --> 00:34:03.147
Me saving things the leech.
Not the eating of it.

00:34:03.258 --> 00:34:06.421
Zoidberg, I'm very surprised
at you, slightly.

00:34:15.203 --> 00:34:18.536
- Psst! Leela.
- Shh! I'm a fugitive.

00:34:18.640 --> 00:34:22.576
I know. I miss you so much, Leela,
even more than when you were here.

00:34:22.978 --> 00:34:24.445
I miss you, too, Fry.

00:34:24.546 --> 00:34:26.810
And you probably think
what I'm doing is wrong.

00:34:26.915 --> 00:34:28.542
But it's something
I really care about...

00:34:28.650 --> 00:34:30.481
You don't have to explain, Leela.

00:34:30.585 --> 00:34:33.452
You're you.
That's all I need to know.

00:34:36.257 --> 00:34:38.725
Goodbye, sweet goofbag.

00:34:51.239 --> 00:34:53.207
I'll miss her, too, buddy.

00:34:53.308 --> 00:34:55.469
- Dibs on her iPod.
- Dibs on...

00:34:58.113 --> 00:35:00.673
Hey, Fry! Long time, man.

00:35:00.782 --> 00:35:02.579
Hey, Hutch! What have you been up to?

00:35:02.684 --> 00:35:04.879
Same old, same old.
Searching the dumpsters,

00:35:04.986 --> 00:35:08.183
protecting my thoughts
with tin foil, peeing myself.

00:35:08.289 --> 00:35:09.688
So, what brings you to Earth?

00:35:09.791 --> 00:35:13.557
It's top secret. Hey, take off
your helmet and I'll think it to you.

00:35:14.062 --> 00:35:16.394
Okay. Here goes.

00:35:42.330 --> 00:35:44.389
Where are you? And me?

00:35:44.499 --> 00:35:49.027
The Great Hall of
the Ancient Legion of Madfellows.

00:35:49.137 --> 00:35:50.104
Welcome, bro.

00:35:50.205 --> 00:35:51.570
- Welcome, bro.
- Welcome, bro.

00:35:51.673 --> 00:35:54.870
Sorry I bashed your
head in, buddy, but I had to.

00:35:54.976 --> 00:35:58.537
You see, the fate of the
universe depends on you.

00:35:58.646 --> 00:36:02.639
- Yeah, I get that a lot.
- The Grand Curator will tell you more.

00:36:02.750 --> 00:36:04.183
Take me to him.

00:36:04.285 --> 00:36:05.912
- Hey, man.
- Hey.

00:36:06.020 --> 00:36:07.578
So dig this, Fry.

00:36:07.689 --> 00:36:11.125
Our commune has been
monitoring the universe's life energy

00:36:11.226 --> 00:36:16.289
for, like, a really long time,
and we're grokking some super weird junk.

00:36:16.664 --> 00:36:19.792
I don't mean to be rude, but it's
kind of hard to take you seriously

00:36:19.901 --> 00:36:22.335
when you say junk
like "grok" and "junk."

00:36:22.437 --> 00:36:25.133
- What about "commune"?
- Especially "commune."

00:36:25.240 --> 00:36:27.936
Come on, it's the fate of
the universe, puff it up a little.

00:36:28.042 --> 00:36:30.169
Like you could say
your ancient order is sensing

00:36:30.278 --> 00:36:32.872
deep upheaval in the
cosmic life energy field.

00:36:35.516 --> 00:36:41.250
Okay. I'll try. So, like,
a really, really long time ago...

00:36:42.824 --> 00:36:44.917
Eons ago!

00:36:46.261 --> 00:36:47.489
Cool.

00:36:47.729 --> 00:36:53.531
Eons ago, the life force we call
Chee permeated the universe.

00:36:55.970 --> 00:37:01.135
The Green Chee generated a great
upwelling of life across the cosmos.

00:37:01.242 --> 00:37:03.836
But then, for reasons unknown...

00:37:03.945 --> 00:37:06.140
Ooh. "Reasons unknown."

00:37:06.247 --> 00:37:09.216
Now that's the sort of hook that
grabs the attention of me, the viewer.

00:37:09.317 --> 00:37:10.841
For reasons unknown...

00:37:10.952 --> 00:37:12.112
Nice.

00:37:12.220 --> 00:37:18.250
...the Chee began to recede,
and the diversity of life began to wither.

00:37:18.359 --> 00:37:20.520
The life forms we know today

00:37:20.628 --> 00:37:25.156
are but a fraction of a fraction of
the magnificence that once existed.

00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:27.033
But a bunch of dudes, right,

00:37:27.135 --> 00:37:30.627
they totally passed this far-out
knowledge down through the ages.

00:37:30.838 --> 00:37:33.432
Some with
this knowledge were called prophets,

00:37:33.541 --> 00:37:39.104
some, fruitcakes. We, the Legion
of Madfellows, are their heirs.

00:37:39.681 --> 00:37:41.012
Hey, I'm on TV.

