species they encountered,

00:54:21.081 --> 00:54:24.380
so they can recreate
them if they go extinct.

00:54:24.685 --> 00:54:30.021
Just as a pillow, a wig and a corncob pipe
can be used to recreate my old girlfriend!

00:54:30.424 --> 00:54:31.413
Bingo.

00:54:33.160 --> 00:54:35.651
Meanwhile, at the Honeybun Hideout.

00:54:41.468 --> 00:54:45.370
There! Now you know how it feels
to be locked up in a go-go cage.

00:54:45.605 --> 00:54:47.232
What the hell are you talking about?

00:54:47.341 --> 00:54:48.774
Shut your man-hole.

00:54:53.914 --> 00:54:55.108
I feel dirty.

00:54:55.515 --> 00:54:57.608
Are you sure Fry is
working for your father?

00:54:57.718 --> 00:55:01.210
It just doesn't seem like him to
be so evil, or to hold down a job.

00:55:01.321 --> 00:55:04.882
It's true, Leela.
Cross My Heart bra and swear to Goddess.

00:55:04.992 --> 00:55:07.483
But the Fry I know
wouldn't do that.

00:55:07.594 --> 00:55:10.927
I'm gonna call his cell phone
telephone and prove you wrong.

00:55:15.469 --> 00:55:17.994
Oh, no! Frida's been murdered!

00:55:20.340 --> 00:55:22.604
Sweet she-cattle of Seattle.

00:55:22.709 --> 00:55:24.574
Not your
strong suit, woman.

00:55:24.678 --> 00:55:26.111
Who could have done this?

00:55:26.213 --> 00:55:27.805
Your dad? Nixon?

00:55:28.315 --> 00:55:29.339
Fry?

00:55:29.449 --> 00:55:31.849
No, never. I don't think.

00:55:31.952 --> 00:55:34.477
Anyhow, there's a crazed
murderer on the loose,

00:55:34.588 --> 00:55:36.988
possibly in the shadows
or hanging from the ceiling.

00:55:38.191 --> 00:55:40.056
So just stay calm while I call Fry.

00:55:44.064 --> 00:55:47.500
So where are the Encyclopods
and the Dark Ones now?

00:55:50.103 --> 00:55:52.571
When the life-giving
Chee receded,

00:55:52.672 --> 00:55:56.108
only the toughest organisms
could adapt and survive,

00:55:56.209 --> 00:55:57.642
like the Dark Ones.

00:56:01.014 --> 00:56:04.313
Many more died out,
like the Encyclopods.

00:56:04.418 --> 00:56:08.149
But, and this is the
great secret of our age,

00:56:08.255 --> 00:56:12.123
we believe they
left an egg behind.

00:56:12.426 --> 00:56:14.587
- Is it edible?
- We're not gonna eat it!

00:56:14.694 --> 00:56:19.427
Not unless we find a second one.
No, Fry, we intend to hatch it!

00:56:19.633 --> 00:56:21.464
And that's where you come in.

00:56:21.568 --> 00:56:23.035
And here I am.

00:56:23.136 --> 00:56:26.264
At long last the tide
of Chee has returned,

00:56:26.373 --> 00:56:29.774
and its nourishing flow
has awakened the dormant egg.

00:56:29.976 --> 00:56:30.943
That's good.

00:56:31.044 --> 00:56:35.572
It's better than good. It's better.
With its massive stash of DNA,

00:56:35.682 --> 00:56:40.710
the Encyclopod can reconstruct
every species that ever went extinct.

00:56:40.821 --> 00:56:46.054
Imagine, all the animals that
failed evolution's test, alive again!

00:56:46.159 --> 00:56:50.493
The dodo bird, the brittle-klutz,
the striped biologist-taunter.

00:56:50.597 --> 00:56:55.125
- So, where is this egg?
- In the violet dwarf star system.

00:56:55.235 --> 00:56:58.636
- And what does it look like?
- A violet dwarf star!

00:56:58.738 --> 00:57:02.936
You mean, the whole star
is a single... Whoa! Sci-fi.

00:57:03.243 --> 00:57:08.579
Alas! Even now, a Dark One is headed
to the star to ensure its destruction.

00:57:08.682 --> 00:57:11.116
Dang! So what does
this Dark One look like?

00:57:12.319 --> 00:57:16.585
We don't know. I admit
it's a horrifically grave situation.

00:57:16.690 --> 00:57:18.282
Don't sugarcoat it, Nine.

00:57:18.391 --> 00:57:20.256
The Dark Ones have
been evolving so long,

00:57:20.360 --> 00:57:22.225
it could be anything or anyone.

00:57:22.329 --> 00:57:23.489
Or anybody.

00:57:23.597 --> 00:57:24.928
You mean, like, people?

00:57:25.031 --> 00:57:27.295
Any people. It will kill the egg,

00:57:27.400 --> 00:57:30.233
and every dude, woman
and child who knows about it.

00:57:30.337 --> 00:57:33.704
Even our crazy caps will
be useless at close range.

00:57:33.974 --> 00:57:38.240
That's why only you, with your
defective unreadable brainwave,

00:57:38.345 --> 00:57:39.812
may be able to thwart them

00:57:39.913 --> 00:57:43.212
and usher in a new
green age of wonder and...

00:57:45.785 --> 00:57:48.345
You're on Fry-time. Leela!

00:57:48.755 --> 00:57:51.223
- Did you get my message?
- What message?

00:57:51.324 --> 00:57:52.916
Didn't you see Frida Waterfall?

00:57:53.026 --> 00:57:55.551
So you did
kill Frida Waterfall?

00:57:55.762 --> 00:57:58.253
What? No. I told her
to tell you that I'm...

00:57:58.632 --> 00:58:01.999
Oh, Jeep! The Dark Ones
got her. It's all true.

00:58:02.402 --> 00:58:04.927
We need to talk, Leela.
Then I can explain...

00:58:05.105 --> 00:58:07.733
Well, I can't explain anything,
but we should talk anyway.

00:58:07.841 --> 00:58:09.968
- Where are you?
- Oh, no.

00:58:10.076 --> 00:58:12.374
I'm not gonna expose
the Honeybun Hideout.

00:58:12.479 --> 00:58:13.571
Where are you?

00:58:13.680 --> 00:58:17.241
Near the Keeler Crater on Mars.
Do you know it?

00:58:17.350 --> 00:58:19.784
I think I read about it.

00:58:20.487 --> 00:58:23.752
I'll meet you at the south
rim in one hour. No mustaches.

00:58:27.761 --> 00:58:32.027
Kif, set coordinates, 36-24-36.

00:58:32.399 --> 00:58:35.266
AKA, Leela.

00:58:43.143 --> 00:58:46.840
Ten minutes late.
Ain't that just like a womanista?

00:58:47.581 --> 00:58:50.709
- Are you alone?
- Of course, don't you trust me?

00:58:54.821 --> 00:58:56.584
There's no escape, Leela.

00:58:56.690 --> 00:58:59.215
If you surrender,
wave your shirt in the air.

00:58:59.392 --> 00:59:00.723
Fry, you traitor!

00:59:02.395 --> 00:59:04.522
Hop onto
the magnet, Leela!

00:59:04.631 --> 00:59:06.462
Okay. One, two...

00:59:20.413 --> 00:59:22.349
I can't believe you
ratted me out, Fry.

00:59:22.616 --> 00:59:24.106
I'm not a rat, I swear.

00:59:24.217 --> 00:59:28.119
If I'm any rodent, it's the loyal
capybara, king of the rats! No, wait.

00:59:31.591 --> 00:59:34.321
This just in, we are about
to get our asses blown off.

00:59:34.427 --> 00:59:36.952
- Labarbara?
- That's right, Linda.

00:59:38.832 --> 00:59:42.290
Stay strong, ladies. We can lose them
in the giant miniature golf course.

00:59:42.402 --> 00:59:45.269
But the course isn't finished.
And there's no girls allowed.

00:59:45.372 --> 00:59:46.566
Fore!

00:59:52.779 --> 00:59:57.648
So, they want to play mini golf, eh?
Two can play at that game.

00:59:57.784 --> 01:00:00.776
Or even four, depending on
the number of ball colors available.

01:00:02.122 --> 01:00:05.717
- I choose pink.
- That's their color, sir.

01:00:05.825 --> 01:00:06.985
The hell it is.

01:00:19.506 --> 01:00:22.771
They're gaining on us.
We need a birdie on the windmill hole.

01:00:24.744 --> 01:00:26.405
Wait. Wait.

01:00:27.781 --> 01:00:29.078
Drop the boot!

01:00:33.987 --> 01:00:35.113
Sir, at our present speed,

01:00:35.221 --> 01:00:38.884
the computer predicts
a 100% chance we'll be sliced in half.

01:00:38.992 --> 01:00:40.016
We'll never make it.

01:00:40.126 --> 01:00:43.823
Not with that attitude, we won't.
Same speed ahead!

01:00:52.739 --> 01:00:55.503
We made it through, Kif.
How many men did we lose?

01:00:55.608 --> 01:00:56.575
All of them.

01:00:56.676 --> 01:00:59.042
Well, at least they won't
have to mourn each other.

01:00:59.145 --> 01:01:02.273
Seal the airlocks,
and draw the shades.

01:01:03.316 --> 01:01:04.647
Resume shooting.

01:01:12.625 --> 01:01:15.423
Oh, no! The gorilla! That's a par-four!

01:01:16.696 --> 01:01:19.392
The mouth's too dangerous.
I'm going for the nose.

01:01:19.499 --> 01:01:22.559
Don't be a sucker. You won't
come out anywhere near the hole.

01:01:22.669 --> 01:01:25.900
You need to aim for the jaws
just when they start to close.

01:01:26.005 --> 01:01:28.473
Start to close?
Are you out of your...

01:01:37.484 --> 01:01:38.849
We made it!

01:01:42.055 --> 01:01:45.218
Captaining 101. Go for the nose.

01:01:50.797 --> 01:01:53.925
My arms are broken,
I'll never paint again.

01:01:55.435 --> 01:01:57.460
You can't sue the military.

01:01:57.570 --> 01:01:59.128
I'm okay then.

01:01:59.572 --> 01:02:00.596
Damage report.

01:02:00.707 --> 01:02:03.403
We lost all remaining
food and oxygen, Captain.

01:02:03.510 --> 01:02:05.637
As well as our XM Radio antenna.

01:02:05.745 --> 01:02:07.178
Then this chase is over.

01:02:07.280 --> 01:02:10.613
Kif, set course
for the nearest XM repair facility.

01:02:10.717 --> 01:02:13.618
Meanwhile, we shall
sing top hits from the '80s.

01:02:13.720 --> 01:02:15.415
Which '80s, sir?

01:02:15.522 --> 01:02:17.854
For me, there are only one '80s.

01:02:19.426 --> 01:02:22.327
Smell like I sound
I'm lost and I'm found

01:02:23.630 --> 01:02:27.794
And I'm hungry like the wolf

01:02:35.842 --> 01:02:39.403
The shot was too good!
We're jamming straight for the hole.

01:02:39.512 --> 01:02:41.343
We're gonna crash, even.

01:02:41.448 --> 01:02:46.010
Shmeesh, shmill out,
shmeverybody. It's a wormhole hole.

01:02:46.486 --> 01:02:51.924
Of course, a wormhole!
We'll simply disappear and reappear in

01:02:54.327 --> 01:02:56.090
another part of the universe.

01:02:56.196 --> 01:02:57.288
We made it!

01:03:03.102 --> 01:03:06.503
Crud nuggets!
We de-spaced right next to the Nimbus.

01:03:06.606 --> 01:03:10.303
Just when you think the chase
is over, it gets twice as exciting!

01:03:19.819 --> 01:03:21.343
Hey, look at that.

01:03:21.454 --> 01:03:23.081
Well, well, well.

01:03:23.456 --> 01:03:26.220
My bloodhound-like instincts
must have hunted them down

01:03:26.326 --> 01:03:29.762
while my other parts
were throbbing to Duran Duran.

01:03:30.063 --> 01:03:33.726
Shall I initiate a pointless
and potentially fatal pursuit?

01:03:33.867 --> 01:03:34.856
Make it so.

01:03:34.968 --> 01:03:37.732
It's gonna be fun on a bun, in space.

01:03:50.583 --> 01:03:54.576
Look! The asteroid.
Now it's crawling with life.

01:03:54.954 --> 01:03:56.649
Like Zoidberg's sandals!

01:03:56.990 --> 01:04:00.084
Wow! It's incredible.

01:04:00.293 --> 01:04:03.820
But it'll be destroyed when
Leo Wong blows up the violet dwarf.

01:04:04.097 --> 01:04:07.726
- So why are you helping him?
- I can't tell you, Leela.

01:04:08.134 --> 01:04:09.294
You just have to trust me.

01:04:09.402 --> 01:04:10.835
You keep saying that,

01:04:10.937 --> 01:04:12.564
but you have to give me
something to go on or I...

01:04:13.806 --> 01:04:17.037
Out of whale oil. Out of whale oil.

01:04:17.143 --> 01:04:19.941
The out-of-fuel indicator. It's indicating.

01:04:21.748 --> 01:04:26.811
Say, what's that violet-colored
dwarf-like star thing we're drifting into?

01:04:26.920 --> 01:04:28.478
The violet dwarf star!

01:04:30.390 --> 01:04:35.384
Of course. The gorilla was the 18th hole,
so we're headed into the ball return.

01:04:36.195 --> 01:04:37.958
What else now can go wrong?

01:04:42.402 --> 01:04:47.430
Ladies, you're under arrest.
Prepare to be boarded again and again.

01:04:47.907 --> 01:04:50.137
He'll never take me alive.

01:04:53.313 --> 01:04:56.874
Don't give up yet.
I've got one more trick up my sleeve.

01:04:56.983 --> 01:04:59.042
That's exactly the number we need.

01:05:03.856 --> 01:05:05.380
The fairer sex.

01:05:08.261 --> 01:05:12.220
Something's very wrong here,
and yet a little bit right.

01:05:13.399 --> 01:05:15.424
Not so fast, Brannigan.

01:05:16.502 --> 01:05:19.130
Even less fast, feministas!

01:05:21.007 --> 01:05:21.996
Bender?

01:05:22.108 --> 01:05:23.473
All two tons of me.

01:05:26.512 --> 01:05:28.446
Oye, oye, oye.

01:05:28.548 --> 01:05:33.576
All rise for the honorable Chief Justice
D-O-G-G and the Associate Justices.

01:05:39.192 --> 01:05:41.251
Yo. Seat it or beat it.

01:05:42.895 --> 01:05:45.921
The charges against
y'all femditos is murder,

01:05:46.032 --> 01:05:50.332
mayhem, vandalism,
kidnapping and resisting arrest.

01:05:50.570 --> 01:05:52.561
Damn! The big five.

01:05:52.839 --> 01:05:56.002
You may now make your opening.
What you got to say for yourselves?

01:05:56.109 --> 01:05:58.100
May it please the Court...

01:05:58.211 --> 01:06:00.338
I mean, may it plizzle the cozizzle.

01:06:00.580 --> 01:06:03.242
- Proceed.
- These charges are outrageous.

01:06:03.349 --> 01:06:07.752
Our only goal was to save a rare
violet star and its precious ecosystem.

01:06:07.854 --> 01:06:09.947
If protecting the environment is a crime,
then...

01:06:10.056 --> 01:06:12.286
Protecting the environment is a crime.

01:06:12.659 --> 01:06:14.854
I rest my mouth.

01:06:14.961 --> 01:06:17.657
Do you swear to tell the whole
truth and nothing but the truth?

01:06:17.764 --> 01:06:21.894
I... Well, now, I... Am I under
oath when I take the oath?

01:06:22.301 --> 01:06:25.202
Can the witness identify
the feminista leader?

01:06:25.304 --> 01:06:26.532
That's her right there,

01:06:26.639 --> 01:06:29.267
with the "I'm gonna kill
you Bender" look in her eye.

01:06:29.375 --> 01:06:33.106
Hey, aren't you the robot who
robbed me at gunpoint last year?

01:06:33.379 --> 01:06:35.279
No further answers, Your Honor.

01:06:35.882 --> 01:06:39.045
Please, Justice Dogg, Leela and
her friends are completely innocent.

01:06:39.152 --> 01:06:42.519
Hold up. Were you or were
you not abducted by these hoes?

01:06:43.456 --> 01:06:46.289
Well, abducted is such an ugly word.

01:06:46.693 --> 01:06:50.720
Mr. Wong, the court cannot compel you
to testify against your own daughter.

01:06:50.930 --> 01:06:54.889
No. No, I want to. Also, I got
something to say about my wife.

01:06:55.401 --> 01:06:56.368
Aw, yeah.

01:06:59.038 --> 01:07:02.405
Having heard some of the testimony
over these jams I've been listening to,

01:07:02.508 --> 01:07:05.170
me and my crew will
now kick it in the mix.

01:07:28.101 --> 01:07:31.400
All right. We got us
a verdict up in this High Court.

01:07:31.871 --> 01:07:34.499
Bailiff, drop it like
it's legal precedent.

01:07:34.774 --> 01:07:38.835
In the matter of Leo Wong v.
The Greenorita Eco-Feminist Collective,

01:07:38.978 --> 01:07:42.106
four justices vote to convict,
five to acquit.

01:07:43.683 --> 01:07:46.379
However, since the vote was
strictly along gender lines

01:07:46.486 --> 01:07:51.014
and the female justices' votes only
count half, you are hereby found guilty.

01:07:52.625 --> 01:07:56.322
It's a humiliating and biased system,
but it works.

01:07:56.763 --> 01:07:59.926
Fifty years in the maximum
security Dogg house.

01:08:01.267 --> 01:08:02.234
Peace.

01:08:11.544 --> 01:08:17.244
- Ladies! Welcome to hell.
- Beats Nutley on a Saturday night.

01:08:17.350 --> 01:08:23.414
This is a privately-owned for-profit prison,
and I run a tight, cheap ship!

01:08:23.523 --> 01:08:28.153
I've done this by cutting cost everywhere,
especially on punishment.

01:08:28.261 --> 01:08:32.925
I rely on you inmates to make
prison unpleasant for yourselves.

01:08:33.032 --> 01:08:35.432
You're encouraged to
sexually harass new prisoners,

01:08:35.535 --> 01:08:40.029
organize no-holds-barred
catfights and maintain poor hygiene.

01:08:40.139 --> 01:08:42.232
Try and make me, copper.

01:08:42.341 --> 01:08:44.241
A troublemaker.

01:08:45.511 --> 01:08:48.241
Taste the lash of my
99-cent-store nightstick!

01:08:51.751 --> 01:08:52.979
Yee-ha!

01:08:53.085 --> 01:08:56.316
With the feministas in
jail, it full speed ahead.

01:08:57.023 --> 01:09:00.550
You and me, Fry. We implode
the violet dwarf star tomorrow.

01:09:00.660 --> 01:09:01.684
Ka-boom-boom.

01:09:01.794 --> 01:09:03.261
- You and me?
- Yeah.

01:09:03.362 --> 01:09:04.852
- Tomorrow?
- Tomorrow.

01:09:04.964 --> 01:09:07.057
- Ka-boom?
- Ka-boom-boom.

01:09:15.241 --> 01:09:18.373
Hello? Madfellows? I need to...

01:09:21.013 --> 01:09:23.982
Okay, Leo Wong's about to
destroy the violet dwarf.

01:09:24.083 --> 01:09:26.574
So, whatever I need to know
to stop him, tell me now.

01:09:26.686 --> 01:09:29.519
Alas! Stopping Wong
isn't the only problem.

01:09:29.622 --> 01:09:32.648
One of the Dark Ones will try to
stop you from stopping him.

01:09:32.758 --> 01:09:35.727
So, you must stop it from
stopping you from stopping him.

01:09:35.828 --> 01:09:37.728
But how can I stop
it stop me stop him?

01:09:37.830 --> 01:09:41.459
Stop it! Behold,
the Omega Device.

01:09:44.670 --> 01:09:45.637
That's it?

01:09:45.738 --> 01:09:49.230
The name "Omega Device" sort of
conjured up something cooler-looking.

01:09:49.342 --> 01:09:51.367
Not that I'm disappointed or anything.

01:09:51.477 --> 01:09:54.378
The important thing is what's inside.

01:09:54.480 --> 01:09:57.210
- What does that look like?
- No one knows, man.

01:09:57.316 --> 01:09:59.113
It was invented
by a blind inventor,

01:09:59.218 --> 01:10:02.051
and the one dude he
described it to was deaf.

01:10:02.154 --> 01:10:04.088
So the legend goes.

01:10:04.390 --> 01:10:09.191
When activated, the device will emit
a localized blast of delta-band noise

01:10:09.295 --> 01:10:11.820
to momentarily
disable the Dark One.

01:10:11.931 --> 01:10:14.195
- Like farting in a tent?
- No, an elevator.

01:10:14.300 --> 01:10:17.929
Which is why you must
strike the enemy at point blank range!

01:10:19.438 --> 01:10:22.100
But the Dark One could
look like anything or anyone, right?

01:10:22.208 --> 01:10:23.698
Or anywhere.

01:10:23.976 --> 01:10:25.807
So, what's your plan to recognize it?

01:10:25.912 --> 01:10:27.539
- We don't have one.
- Got it.

01:10:27.647 --> 01:10:29.842
And we don't dare
think of one neither.

01:10:29.949 --> 01:10:33.646
'Cause if we do, the Dark Ones
might sense kind of the general vibe.

01:10:33.886 --> 01:10:36.218
Even through our mighty foil.

01:10:36.489 --> 01:10:39.947
Oh, man!
Anyone got some tape or some gum?

01:10:40.092 --> 01:10:44.290
As my colleague indicated,
the plan cannot come from us, Fry.

01:10:44.397 --> 01:10:45.796
We were counting on you

01:10:45.898 --> 01:10:48.526
and your unreadable brain
to come up with something.

01:10:48.634 --> 01:10:50.966
- That was a mistake.
- I see that now.

01:10:51.070 --> 01:10:56.235
Freaky thing is, the Dark Ones'
thoughts are unreadable, just like yours.

01:10:56.342 --> 01:10:59.106
Yes, if we dared unwrap our heads,

01:10:59.211 --> 01:11:04.478
we could easily locate the one other being
whose mind we can't read. The Dark One!

01:11:04.617 --> 01:11:06.915
But then the Dark One
would read our minds

01:11:07.019 --> 01:11:09.351
and crush them
like blood pumpkins.

01:11:09.455 --> 01:11:12.891
Wait. I can read minds
and my mind can't be read.

01:11:13.225 --> 01:11:15.022
- I have a plan.
- Great.

01:11:15.127 --> 01:11:16.822
Whatever it is, don't tell us.

01:11:16.929 --> 01:11:21.025
Wait. Fry can read minds
and his mind can't be read.

01:11:21.233 --> 01:11:23.895
So he can safely
scan for the Dark One...

01:11:24.003 --> 01:11:25.402
Shut up! Shut up!

01:11:37.783 --> 01:11:42.686
Leela, time is running out.
We must get to the violet star.

01:11:42.788 --> 01:11:44.722
Okay, okay. Shut up, already.

01:11:44.857 --> 01:11:46.051
Huh?

01:11:46.158 --> 01:11:47.682
Nobody's talking, Leela.

01:11:47.793 --> 01:11:50.626
We're just painting each other's
toenails with rat blood.

01:11:50.730 --> 01:11:52.197
Lights out, ladies!

01:11:52.298 --> 01:11:55.131
Those compact fluorescent
bulbs waste pennies a day.

01:11:58.871 --> 01:12:00.771
Okay, feministas, all clear.

01:12:00.873 --> 01:12:02.465
Whoa!

01:12:02.575 --> 01:12:05.476
We now go live to Leela
with the escape plan.

01:12:05.578 --> 01:12:06.909
- Leela?
- Thanks, Linda.

01:12:07.013 --> 01:12:10.210
Now we're in here because we
tried to save endangered wildlife.

01:12:10.316 --> 01:12:13.547
So this time,
endangered wildlife will save us.

01:12:14.987 --> 01:12:16.921
The Martian muck leech.

01:12:17.023 --> 01:12:20.459
That's right. He's been living
off me since we got captured.

01:12:21.660 --> 01:12:24.060
Little cutie almost sucked me dry.

01:12:32.371 --> 01:12:34.066
Look at him go.

01:12:34.173 --> 01:12:37.540
Like a green snake
through a sugarcane cake.

01:12:37.643 --> 01:12:39.702
Keep trying.

01:12:48.154 --> 01:12:53.319
Our top story. The universe's most wanted
eco-feminists are now behind bars,

01:12:53.426 --> 01:12:58.363
including gang leader, Turanga Leela.
AKA, the Notorious B-I-Itch.

01:12:59.865 --> 01:13:02.925
We finished un-pinking
the ship, Hubert. Now what?

01:13:03.035 --> 01:13:04.559
Now we get back to work.

01:13:04.670 --> 01:13:08.071
And if that means destroying
an ecosystem or two, so be it.

01:13:08.340 --> 01:13:12.401
I just meant without our good
friends Fry, Leela, Amy and the robot.

01:13:12.511 --> 01:13:17.107
Oh, boo-hoo. This is a business,
not a social club. Money talks.

01:13:17.683 --> 01:13:20.447
True wealth is
measured in friendships.

01:13:20.553 --> 01:13:21.850
Shut up, you.

01:13:21.954 --> 01:13:23.649
Life goes on.

01:13:23.756 --> 01:13:27.453
But I believe we'll forever
carry the pain on the inside.

01:13:34.600 --> 01:13:38.934
Oh, no, a rooster!
That indicates it's the following morning.

01:13:41.006 --> 01:13:43.600
How's that creepy crawler doing?

01:13:43.709 --> 01:13:47.110
I'm sorry, femi-sisters,
but it pooped out around 3:00 a.m.

01:13:47.213 --> 01:13:49.477
Poor thing couldn't take another bite.

01:13:51.417 --> 01:13:53.214
Well, I guess we failed.

01:13:53.319 --> 01:13:56.880
But what matters is, we tried our
best and we looked good doing it.

01:14:01.760 --> 01:14:03.853
Bender, is that you?

01:14:03.963 --> 01:14:06.761
Who does it look like?
My identical cousin Buster?

01:14:06.866 --> 01:14:07.890
Yes.

01:14:09.101 --> 01:14:13.401
You're here to break us out?
But you're the one who put us in.

01:14:13.506 --> 01:14:16.566
But I'm Bender,
king of the combination shot.

01:14:16.675 --> 01:14:21.703
I put you in so that by busting you out,
I could commit 15 felonies at once.

01:14:21.881 --> 01:14:26.079
Put my rap sheet miles ahead
of yours on the all-time chart.

01:14:26.252 --> 01:14:28.584
You are one devious bastard.

01:14:28.687 --> 01:14:31.155
That's what it says on my vanity plate.

01:14:38.764 --> 01:14:41.699
- What about the sentries?
- Already taken care of.

01:14:41.834 --> 01:14:45.736
I sent them a cake laced with nutmeg.
That's a human sleeping drug, right?

01:14:45.838 --> 01:14:48.500
No, it's a human baking drug.

01:14:49.942 --> 01:14:53.969
Okay, Plan B. Everyone knows
men have one fatal weakness,

01:14:54.079 --> 01:14:58.038
they can't resist hookers.
Dixie, Trixie, you know what to do.

01:15:06.058 --> 01:15:07.821
Hello, boys!

01:15:10.229 --> 01:15:13.494
Your eyes say no,
but your machine gun fire says...

01:15:35.254 --> 01:15:37.654
Ladies and gentleman
and whatever,

01:15:37.756 --> 01:15:41.749
welcome to my most environmentally
disastrous implosion ever.

01:15:41.994 --> 01:15:43.859
A whole star system!

01:15:47.299 --> 01:15:51.065
Kif, old boy, mind if I sit on
your shoulders for a better view?

01:15:51.170 --> 01:15:53.968
Well, actually, sir, I was hoping...

01:15:54.073 --> 01:15:55.165
Thanks.

01:15:56.475 --> 01:16:02.004
My associate Philip Fry here will have
honor to blow this ugly, dirty star

01:16:02.114 --> 01:16:04.014
into nice, clean black hole.

01:16:08.053 --> 01:16:12.114
Fry, careful those wires.
What you doing down there?

01:16:12.224 --> 01:16:15.125
Just polishing your shoes, Mr. W.

01:16:18.063 --> 01:16:21.590
That nice. Get between
the toes there, very dirty.

01:16:26.605 --> 01:16:28.800
Well, so much for Plan B.

01:16:28.907 --> 01:16:29.999
What's Plan C?

01:16:30.109 --> 01:16:34.102
All situations have the same Plan C.
Bending, come on.

01:16:42.488 --> 01:16:45.389
We're boned, Bender.
It's a brick wall.

01:16:45.491 --> 01:16:49.188
Granted, it's not on
the list of approved bendables,

01:16:49.295 --> 01:16:55.791
but I'm so great!

01:17:01.707 --> 01:17:04.232
Dogs! The boning continues.

01:17:05.311 --> 01:17:08.769
Green Bluebird, this is Mr. Fabulous.
We are go for cheesing it.

01:17:26.365 --> 01:17:29.960
Professor! Hermes! Zoidberg!

01:17:32.404 --> 01:17:34.167
Scruffy. A janitor.

01:17:34.373 --> 01:17:35.567
You helped us escape?

01:17:35.674 --> 01:17:39.508
Even after we locked you in a go-go
cage like common go-go dancers?

01:17:39.611 --> 01:17:45.447
I couldn't live with myself, Leela.
I call myself a scientist,

01:17:45.551 --> 01:17:49.112
wear the white coat and probe
a monkey every now and again,

01:17:49.355 --> 01:17:53.689
yet I put monetary gain
ahead of preserving nature.

01:17:53.792 --> 01:17:56.056
Can you ever forgive me?

01:17:56.795 --> 01:17:57.784
I reckon.

01:17:57.896 --> 01:18:02.299
- I could kiss you, Professor.
- Okay, but watch out for my new grill.

01:18:10.209 --> 01:18:13.303
Before the grand finale, as it were,

01:18:13.412 --> 01:18:17.212
it seems only fitting that I,
Commodore 64 Zapp Brannigan,

01:18:17.316 --> 01:18:19.375
say a few brief pages in honor of...

01:18:19.485 --> 01:18:23.387
Whatever your plan is,
Fry, I suggest you get on with it.

01:18:23.555 --> 01:18:26.456
Get... Shoot, I got hot
sauce on my Number 9 shirt.

01:18:26.925 --> 01:18:31.692
Okay, locate the Dark One by finding
someone whose thoughts I can't read.

01:18:32.164 --> 01:18:33.165
And unaccustomed...

01:18:33.399 --> 01:18:36.800
By God!
I'm the greatest speaker of all time.

01:18:36.902 --> 01:18:40.360
They're suckling at the
teats of my every syllable.

01:18:40.472 --> 01:18:41.734
Allow me now...

01:18:42.408 --> 01:18:46.606
His voice is like ear sandpaper.
I miss Amy.

01:18:47.045 --> 01:18:48.876
The one secret
no one ever suspected

01:18:48.981 --> 01:18:51.449
is that I really did
stage the moon landing.

01:18:52.084 --> 01:18:53.108
On Venus.

01:18:55.621 --> 01:19:00.991
If I had all the money
in the world, I'd... Oh, wait. I do.

01:19:03.295 --> 01:19:07.698
I'd like to thank the academy,
my agent, and most of all,

01:19:07.833 --> 01:19:12.065
my operating system,
Windows Vista, for everything it...

01:19:12.171 --> 01:19:13.536
System error.

01:19:13.639 --> 01:19:16.437
Naked ladies. Naked ladies.
Naked ladies. Naked ladies.

01:19:16.542 --> 01:19:20.706
I never should have taken that accent
elimination class from Jackie Chan.

01:19:21.180 --> 01:19:24.616
And so, as we obliterize this star,

01:19:24.716 --> 01:19:29.585
let us remember those immortal words
once spoken by a great man, moi.

01:19:29.688 --> 01:19:33.021
And I quote, "All good
things must come to an end,

01:19:33.125 --> 01:19:35.389
"preferably in
a humongous explosion."

01:19:37.529 --> 01:19:39.463
Let's pop this beach ball.

01:19:40.165 --> 01:19:42.497
Ten! Nine!

01:19:43.268 --> 01:19:44.758
Eight!

01:19:48.907 --> 01:19:50.807
There's no one here whose
thoughts can't be read.

01:19:50.909 --> 01:19:53.935
No one, except me!

01:19:54.313 --> 01:19:57.680
My thoughts can't be read.
But that's crazy.

01:19:57.816 --> 01:20:00.910
If I were the Dark One,
I'd know it, wouldn't I?

01:20:01.820 --> 01:20:04.618
But, here I am, right where
the Dark One would be,

01:20:04.723 --> 01:20:06.554
about to blow up the star.

01:20:06.658 --> 01:20:10.059
Oh, God! Somewhere deep
inside of me, it's me!

01:20:10.162 --> 01:20:11.390
I'm the Dark One!

01:20:15.133 --> 01:20:16.828
Put your hands in the air!

01:20:17.703 --> 01:20:19.671
Should we wave them
like we just don't care?

01:20:19.771 --> 01:20:21.398
That's optional.

01:20:22.241 --> 01:20:26.871
You girl punks gone too far this time.
Your parents should be ashamed.

01:20:27.012 --> 01:20:28.479
Yes, you should!

01:20:30.749 --> 01:20:33.081
- Amy?
- Amy!

01:20:33.185 --> 01:20:35.551
Destroy the star, Leo, hurry.

01:20:35.654 --> 01:20:37.884
You got it, Mr. Voice-in-my-head.

01:20:46.465 --> 01:20:50.401
I've gotta admit, Amy,
you got a pretty good swing.

01:20:51.403 --> 01:20:53.871
Really? Thanks, Dad.

01:20:55.974 --> 01:20:59.307
Okay, time to defuse
this star cracker once and for all.

01:21:00.612 --> 01:21:02.705
Leela, wait.
You're making a mistake.

01:21:02.814 --> 01:21:04.839
You have no idea
what's really going on.

01:21:04.950 --> 01:21:06.577
What is really going on?

01:21:06.685 --> 01:21:07.709
I can't tell you.

01:21:07.819 --> 01:21:10.310
Then why should I trust you? Why?

01:21:10.422 --> 01:21:12.982
Because... Because...

01:21:20.299 --> 01:21:22.995
You're you. That's all I need to know.

01:21:23.969 --> 01:21:25.800
- No! Don't do it!
- Fiddlesticks.

01:21:25.904 --> 01:21:28.031
Leela, are you crazy?

01:21:28.140 --> 01:21:31.303
We became fugitives
and jail-breakers to stop him.

01:21:31.410 --> 01:21:33.708
And hookers, don't forget hookers.

01:21:33.812 --> 01:21:35.143
Shame on all of you.

01:21:35.247 --> 01:21:38.239
After everything we've been through
together, do you really think Fry would...

01:21:43.822 --> 01:21:47.815
Goodbye, Leela.
I destroy myself to save you.

01:21:58.103 --> 01:22:01.231
Where's the boom?
I was expecting a boom.

01:22:01.440 --> 01:22:05.240
It didn't work. I'm the Dark One,
and it didn't do anything.

01:22:05.344 --> 01:22:08.211
You're not the Dark One, I am.

01:22:08.313 --> 01:22:09.507
Leela?

01:22:09.615 --> 01:22:11.708
Not Leela, you moron. Me!

01:22:13.619 --> 01:22:15.382
What did you do to me?

01:22:17.155 --> 01:22:18.144
Ew!

01:22:18.991 --> 01:22:22.654
I am the Dark One.
The very last Dark One.

01:22:22.894 --> 01:22:26.227
How is it possible
I couldn't read your mind?

01:22:26.999 --> 01:22:30.059
Oh, I am momentarily disabled.

01:22:38.844 --> 01:22:41.904
What's happening out there?

01:22:42.014 --> 01:22:43.914
Somethings wondersful.

01:23:05.270 --> 01:23:09.798
The star and the asteroid.
They were an egg and a sperm.

01:23:09.908 --> 01:23:13.435
Great modem of mercy.
Cover the children's eyes.

01:23:13.545 --> 01:23:14.876
There are no children here.

01:23:14.980 --> 01:23:17.141
Then move your fat head.
I can't see.

01:23:31.296 --> 01:23:36.233
The Encyclopod is reborn.
A new green age has begun!

01:23:36.334 --> 01:23:38.564
So the legend foretold.

01:23:48.447 --> 01:23:53.475
Look! Inside its pouch.
Extinct Tasmanian tigers.

01:23:53.785 --> 01:23:56.811
And dodo birds.
- And white rhinos.

01:23:56.922 --> 01:23:59.686
And striped biologist-taunters.

01:23:59.791 --> 01:24:01.986
What are you gonna do, shoot us?

01:24:07.232 --> 01:24:08.199
Life!

01:24:10.802 --> 01:24:16.001
These once extinct plants
and animals are my gift to the universe.

01:24:16.341 --> 01:24:20.505
Through untold generations,
my race has treasured their DNA.

01:24:20.946 --> 01:24:25.542
Treat them wisely with the knowledge
that all species are precious.

01:24:25.884 --> 01:24:29.115
This is unbelievable. What's going on?

01:24:29.221 --> 01:24:32.088
To answer that, I must tell you a story.

01:24:32.324 --> 01:24:35.691
A story of two alien
species so ancient that...

01:24:40.098 --> 01:24:44.535
- Hutch, are you okay?
- My sister's femi-necklace.

01:24:44.636 --> 01:24:45.660
What?

01:24:48.039 --> 01:24:50.564
Hey, how come I can't
read your thoughts anymore?

01:24:51.910 --> 01:24:56.040
I shall avenge you, Hutch Waterfall.

01:25:01.052 --> 01:25:05.648
After all these eons,
the Dark Ones are no more.

01:25:05.757 --> 01:25:10.217
Will you preserve their
DNA, O Great Encyclopod?

01:25:11.696 --> 01:25:14.995
I suppose I should.
Wait, where did it go?

01:25:18.703 --> 01:25:19.670
What?

01:25:19.938 --> 01:25:24.671
Well, at any rate, I shall
preserve the DNA of Homo sapiens.

01:25:30.782 --> 01:25:33.876
I thought you only saved the
DNA of endangered species.

01:25:33.985 --> 01:25:34.952
Farewell.

01:25:37.289 --> 01:25:38.483
I guess he didn't hear me.

01:25:38.590 --> 01:25:42.651
Well, looks like that wraps everything
up in a nice big, old, fat sack of...

01:25:42.761 --> 01:25:47.494
I hereby arrest you
fugitives on 53 counts of fugivity.

01:25:47.599 --> 01:25:51.091
Kif, round them up,
and spare me the weary sigh for once.

01:25:51.937 --> 01:25:52.904
Kif.

01:25:53.805 --> 01:25:55.170
Wait for me.

01:26:08.687 --> 01:26:12.885
Well, this is the end. There was so
many things I wanted to say to you.

01:26:12.991 --> 01:26:14.458
Like what?

01:26:14.559 --> 01:26:18.586
Like this is not the end.
But mostly just, I love you, Leela.

01:26:21.032 --> 01:26:26.060
Maybe I waited too long to say this,
but I love you, too. Wormhole!

01:26:27.305 --> 01:26:30.797
Sweet topology of
cosmology, it's huge!

01:26:30.909 --> 01:26:35.437
If we fly into it, it could take
us trillions of light years away.

01:26:35.547 --> 01:26:38.072
There's no knowing if we'll ever return.

01:26:38.183 --> 01:26:40.549
What do we do?
Should we go for it?

01:26:44.189 --> 01:26:48.421
Into the breach, meatbags.
Or not. Whatever.

01:26:48.526 --> 01:26:51.552
Go, go, go, go,
go, go, go, go, go, go.

01:26:51.663 --> 01:26:54.154
Go, go, go, go, go,
go, go, go, go, go.